/*!
  \page example_cxx_nanoflann_page Comparison between the Nanoflann and Ponca kd-trees

  \section nanoflann_intro_sec Introduction

  This example uses the kd-trees of %Ponca and of
  <a href="https://github.com/jlblancoc/nanoflann" target="_blank">Nanoflann</a> (v1.5.0, shipped with the example) on
  the same data, and compares their API and their performances to collect neighborhoods.

  \subsection nanoflann_compilation_sec Compilation

  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target ponca_nanoflann
  ./build/examples/cpp/nanoflann/ponca_nanoflann
  \endcode

  \section nanoflann_comparison_sec API comparison

  Task              | %Ponca                                                | Nanoflann
  ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | -------------
  KdTree creation   | \snippet ponca_nanoflann.cpp Create Ponca KdTree      | \snippet ponca_nanoflann.cpp Create NanoFlann KdTree
  Range query       | \snippet ponca_nanoflann.cpp Use Ponca KdTree         | \snippet ponca_nanoflann.cpp Use NanoFlann KdTree

  The fitting object is a Ponca::DryFit, an object that filters the neighbors according to their weight (points
  farther than the scale are not counted), but does not perform any other computation:
  \snippet ponca_nanoflann.cpp Define Fit Type

  \section nanoflann_timings_sec Timings

  The example prints the time required to collect the neighbors, and the number of neighbors collected, without
  spatial data structure (*Raw*) and with both kd-trees. For instance:
  \code
Timings:
Raw :       0.168698
Ponca :     0.025475
Nanoflann : 0.027746
Number of neighbors:
Raw :       950618
Ponca :     950618
Nanoflann : 950618
  \endcode

  \section nanoflann_sourcecode_sec Source code

  \include ponca_nanoflann.cpp
 */
